{
  "dom_id": "step-q67051",
  "name": "Question 1",
  "problem": "What is the third term of the expression $-3k+2l-7m+\\frac{2}{3}n?$",
  "worked_solution": "We put an addition symbol $(+)$ between each part and separate using parentheses:\n\n$$\n(-3k)+(2l)+(-7m)+(\\frac{2}{3}n)\n$$\n\nCounting off the terms:\n\n- the first term is $-3k,$\n\n- the second term is $2l,$\n\n- the third term is $-7m,$ and\n\n- the fourth term is $\\frac{2}{3}n.$\n\nIn particular, we are interested in the third term. The third term is $-7m.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
